FEATURE: font-splash-module
DATE: 2026-10-06
SCOPE: add vUX-fontSplash.js, a splash screen whose loader is a word in the
       consumer's font, filled with an animated gradient while the letters fade

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) is the only project affected. Apps that symlink it
(vGet, app.myinvitees.com, sketch-app) get the module on their next page load,
and nothing changes for them unless they import it.

Consumer-visible surface:
  - vUX-fontSplash.js         new module: FontSplash
  - assets/css/fontSplash.css its stylesheet, linked at import
  - src/helpers.js            module registry entry
  - doc/font-splash.md        new guide
  - examples/fontsplash/      new example page

Purely additive. No member was renamed or removed and no existing call
signature changed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT WAS BUILT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

new FontSplash([element]); config.text, font, size, colors, background,
trackColor, caption, animation (fade | flow | breathe | none), speed, fadeSpeed,
stagger, minOpacity, delay, minDuration, fontTimeout, exit (fade | lift | zoom |
none), exitDuration, zIndex, label, onShow, onHide; initialize(), show(),
hide() -> Promise, during(promise) -> Promise, setProgress(0..1 | null),
destroy(), and read-only state and fontStatus.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No test runner exists in vUX. Verified in headless Chrome 149 (Windows Chrome
driven from WSL, results POSTed back to a scratch server):
  - a scratch harness of 48 checks in real time, all passing: validation,
    reveal, letter measurement, ARIA in both modes, live text rebuild, minDuration
    + exit timing, delay suppression, during() value and rejection, container
    mode and position restore, local() face, failed font, fontTimeout reveal at
    ~430ms for a 400ms timeout against a slow endpoint, hide before reveal,
    destroy dropping the FontFace, grapheme splitting, reshow after hide;
  - screenshots of two variants and of the example page at 1280px reviewed;
    only console output was the intended missing-font warning;
  - no page-level horizontal overflow at 390px (scrollWidth checked in an iframe).
Not tested: Firefox, Safari, real network fonts over a slow connection.
